<description>&lt;p&gt;Mexican special forces captured cartel leader El Chapo Isidro in northern Sinaloa after a firefight that left eleven people dead. The operation sparked vehicle burnings on a highway and gunfire that interrupted a local baseball match. The raid has triggered renewed violence linked to the Sinaloa cartel and a surge in migrant caravan movements toward the U.S. border. 37 battle-related deaths were recorded in 1996, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiwAFBVV95cUxNaS0xVWM4dWpacllqX3lQTGlUbUx6YVhleldQWUVfVXg0Q3dReFphcHFUa2N1OWRhNU5SUXBuNEF0VkVpTDByVGhnVWtYdjBuNnMwTE9LRzNtWEhLWmFnSDlTYVFzak1WY1JyeHo5bnFic0thbkFsZjdQX0VOdWxIREROQWRkQVpVU2JLN1FlWk1ubklNcUdfSmlfS1kydTZhNkREODVTell0Z1dpT3BRdHpnOGFpd3BzMWl5Mml4RlQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;WSJ&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;DW.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiwAFBVV95cUxNTGlxVEZUU3JwNEctQmFlMmNrOTBBQWhuTmhrRVZmTzVkQ2laUlZ1MlRtWEZzVFlxQnNtb0N0NEZNQWFzX2p3VUJiTldDeVp0dkUxZVRTcktWWEVTTURuck5memxLTFZRV2FpU2dVemNiVEdOZFZfRUpEeWNUaFl4bWpmRHFrc09PMmlKX3F5NnUySHJTNTctdDhxRVFtVWo1SXp2OWZ0UFN3TFZ3YXlkMHJObmNIVU85TUw4VnRnc0Y?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Guardian&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMioAFBVV95cUxNMmZ3Y0lQNnRXYjBIVXFZTXMwWFVLSEppaFVBTWYyNno5c2ZfOV8wbU5la0pjbmp1TGlSX3M5clhMbUZHNmFwVDN6TUFOd0g2a3JRWHRUT2Zqb3g4YzllV2tWX0ZuME83Qlg2V0plSTBvTk16Si1ENjFmeFJsdU1OcnpWbEJ1NUMwTENfNU9TdHhPeUtTN1ktMG1oRDhzYjd2?oc=5&quot;&gt;The New York Times&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiqwFBVV95cUxOa2RiNXlYT1VFSmc3c